p.src:
Turn the preparation polarizer through $45^\circ$. The transmitted state has equal $x$- and $y$-components: $\ket{d_+}
  =\frac{\ket{x}+\ket{y}}{\sqrt2}
  =\frac{1}{\sqrt2}
    \begin{pmatrix}1\\1\end{pmatrix}.$ Its orthogonal companion, the backslash polarization, can be chosen as $\ket{d_-}
  =\frac{\ket{x}-\ket{y}}{\sqrt2}
  =\frac{1}{\sqrt2}
    \begin{pmatrix}1\\-1\end{pmatrix}.$ Putting the minus sign on the other component multiplies the whole state by $-1$ and changes no physics. Directly, $\braket{d_-}{d_+}=\frac12(1-1)=0.$

