p.src:
Let the transmission axis make angle $\theta$ with the $x$-axis. Its state and orthogonal partner are $\begin{aligned}
  \ket{\theta}
    &=\cos\theta\,\ket{x}+\sin\theta\,\ket{y}
      \\
    &=
      \begin{pmatrix}
        \cos\theta\\
        \sin\theta
      \end{pmatrix},
      \\
  \ket{\theta_\perp}
    &=\ket{\theta+\pi/2}
      =-\sin\theta\,\ket{x}+\cos\theta\,\ket{y}
      \\
    &=
      \begin{pmatrix}
        -\sin\theta\\
        \cos\theta
      \end{pmatrix}.
      \end{aligned}$ Both have unit norm, and $\braket{\theta}{\theta_\perp}
  =-\cos\theta\sin\theta+\sin\theta\cos\theta=0.$ Also $\ket{\theta+\pi}=-\ket{\theta}$, confirming that a linear polarization axis has period $\pi$, not $2\pi$.

