p.src:
The transition amplitude is $\begin{aligned}
  \braket{\beta}{\alpha}
  &=
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \cos\beta&\sin\beta
  \end{pmatrix}
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \cos\alpha\\
    \sin\alpha
  \end{pmatrix}\\
  &=\cos\alpha\cos\beta+\sin\alpha\sin\beta\\
  &=\cos(\alpha-\beta).
  \end{aligned}$ Therefore the single-photon form of Malus’s law is $\boxed{\operatorname{Prob}(\beta|\alpha)
  =|\braket{\beta}{\alpha}|^2
  =\cos^2(\alpha-\beta).}$

