Let $c=\cos\theta$ and $s=\sin\theta$. Acting on the proposed $+1$ eigenvector gives $\begin{aligned}
  \hat P_\theta
  \begin{pmatrix}c\\s\end{pmatrix}
  &=
  \begin{pmatrix}
    c^2-s^2&2sc\\
    2sc&s^2-c^2
  \end{pmatrix}
  \begin{pmatrix}c\\s\end{pmatrix}\\
  &=
  \begin{pmatrix}
    c(c^2+s^2)\\
    s(c^2+s^2)
  \end{pmatrix}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}c\\s\end{pmatrix}.
  \end{aligned}$

