p.src:
Real coefficients describe every linear polarization, but not every vector in a complex two-dimensional Hilbert space. Consider $\ket{c_+}
  =\frac{1}{\sqrt2}
    \begin{pmatrix}1\\i\end{pmatrix},
  \qquad
  \ket{c_-}
  =\frac{1}{\sqrt2}
    \begin{pmatrix}1\\-i\end{pmatrix}.$ Complex conjugation is essential: $\braket{c_+}{c_+}
  =\frac12\bigl(1+(-i)i\bigr)=1,$ and $\braket{c_-}{c_+}
  =\frac12\bigl(1+i^2\bigr)=0.$ The tempting product without conjugating the bra gives the wrong answer.

